# Task 149-009: Auditor Stale Alert Race Condition Fix

## Problem
Sprint 148 bug: Auditor generates "stale worker" alert for tasks in ASSIGNED/PENDING/CLAIMED state.
Root cause: scanHeartbeats() line 294 only checks DONE/NO_GO — it should also skip non-EXECUTING states.

## Solution
1. In `scanHeartbeats()` (src/monitor/auditor.ts line 293-296), expand the task status check:
   - Only generate stale alerts for tasks in EXECUTING state
   - PENDING, CLAIMED, ASSIGNED → skip (not yet started)
   - DONE, NO_GO → already handled (downgrade to WARNING)

2. Create `src/core/heartbeat-types.ts` as specified in task scope (even though types are in types.ts, we add task-status-aware typing)

3. Write tests in tests/orchestra/auditor-stale-race.test.ts

## Files to Modify
- src/monitor/auditor.ts (patch scanHeartbeats)
- src/core/heartbeat-types.ts (NEW - re-export convenience types)
- tests/orchestra/auditor-stale-race.test.ts (NEW - 5 tests)

## Key Insight
The fix location is line 293-296 in scanHeartbeats(). Currently it reads task.json and only checks isCompleted (DONE/NO_GO). We add an earlier check: if task status is NOT in EXECUTING/TESTING/DOCUMENTING, skip stale check entirely.
